A||||8||Zack Doyle||Is my transmission blown||||9||
Z||000000||Zack Doyle||12-20-2001||05:44 PM||||I woke up this mourning, started my car, but the stick wouldn't shift.  It was stuck in 1st.  So I thought well maybe if it warms up it will be better.  Nope.  the damn thing was stuck.  I turned the car off and forced it into neutral then started it again and tried to put it in to 1st, it wouldn't go.  Then tried in all of the other gears still no luck.  I said screw it and started walking to school.  I get home same thing happens.  I look in the back and pull on the throttle and see small traces of smoke.  I noticed it before but dad said it was water vapor.  But it had a real bad smell.  <P>Any advice or letting me know if I am SOL will be appreciated||||reg||9
Z||000001||ray b||12-20-2001||06:19 PM||||cables are the first thing to check<BR>see if you can move the cable end on the trans bracket<BR>clean and clear junk under/around shifter<BR>you may have droped a pen or something down there<BR>start eazy work to the hard stuff last<BR>spray lube before droping big parts out!!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Zack Doyle||12-20-2001||06:44 PM||||The gears are only stuck when the car is running.  When it is off the stick goes right into the gear.||||reg||8
Z||000003||jelly2m8||12-20-2001||07:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Zack Doyle:<BR><B>The gears are only stuck when the car is running.  When it is off the stick goes right into the gear.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You have a clutch problem. Probably more of a clutch hydraulic problem.<P> Sounds like air in the hydraulics.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Zack Doyle||12-20-2001||07:23 PM||||I had a new cluch put in only 4 months ago.  Could it be giving me problems already??||||reg||8
Z||000005||Mach10||12-20-2001||07:32 PM||||clutch replacement is for slipping problems. Sounds like you aren't releasing... I.E. Hydraulic problems  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000006||DRH||12-20-2001||10:41 PM||||First thing, check the clutch fluid level (in the front compartment, next to the brake cylinder). If it's not full, you've probably got a leak. Check for fluid inside the car under the carpet next to the steering column.<P>Some models have an aluminum clutch pedal arm which can bend and not push the master cylinder in all the way. A magnet will tell you which you have.<P>Have someone else push the clutch and watch to see if the clutch slave cylinder moves backwards. This would mean a broken bracket or loose bolts. <P>The arm going into the bell housing should move about 1" when the clutch is pushed in. If it doesn't, and everything above was OK, you probably have air in the line. If the fluid wasn't low it's probably from a bad slave cylinder. You may still be able to bleed it and have it work for a while. <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>www.v8archie.com</A>  has a good procedure for bleeding. <P>If it's moving 1"... Repost for the bad news...||||reg||1
Z||000007||Rumor||12-21-2001||12:40 AM||||Does this sound familiar:<P>(props go out to oliver Scholz)<P>If your car comes to a stop and the engine stalls, but restarts (in neutral), and immediately stalls again if you put it in drive, your TCC is shot. You can verify this by disconnecting the plug facing forward on the transmission near the oxygen sensor. If the symptoms go away, your TCC is bad. (If the symptoms stay your TCC may still be bad). This is caused by sediment sticking to to the electromagnetic portion of the solenoid. The part number of a replacement solenoid with an improved seal is P/N 8652379. <P>Replacing the TCC seems difficult at first, but it can be done with the transmission still in the car. <P>If you need The instructions as to what to do, let me know...<P>Hope this helps.<BR>-Rumor<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||TylerB11||12-21-2001||01:11 AM||||Rumor - Thats for an AT. Manual transmissions don't have a torque converter solinoid.||||reg||1
